# Telegram Group Management

Lux provides group-management helpers for Telegram bots that need repeatable
moderation, permission, channel-posting, and admin-audit workflows.

## Permission Templates

```elixir
alias Lux.Integrations.Telegram.GroupManager

{:ok, permissions} =
  GroupManager.member_permissions(:read_only, %{
    can_invite_users: true
  })

permissions.can_send_messages
permissions.can_invite_users
```

## Restrict Members

```elixir
{:ok, action} =
  GroupManager.restrict_member(-100123, 42, :read_only, %{
    until_date: 1_800_000_000,
    use_independent_chat_permissions: true
  })

action.endpoint
action.payload.permissions
```

The action can be executed through the Telegram client:

```elixir
Lux.Integrations.Telegram.Client.request(action.method, action.endpoint, %{
  json: action.payload
})
```

## Ban and Unban

```elixir
GroupManager.ban_member("@group", 42, %{revoke_messages: true})
GroupManager.unban_member("@group", 42, %{only_if_banned: true})
```

## Promote Admins

```elixir
GroupManager.promote_member("@channel", 42, :publisher, %{
  custom_title: "Publisher"
})
```

## Default Chat Permissions

```elixir
GroupManager.set_chat_permissions("@group", :media_allowed)
```

## Channel Posts

```elixir
GroupManager.channel_post("@channel", "release notes", %{
  parse_mode: "MarkdownV2",
  disable_notification: true
})
```

## Admin Audit Logs

```elixir
GroupManager.admin_log_entry(:restrict_member, %{
  actor_id: 1,
  target_user_id: 42,
  chat_id: -100123,
  reason: "spam burst",
  metadata: %{duration: 3600}
})
```

Persist these entries in the caller's store so moderation actions can be
reviewed or replayed independently from Telegram API responses.
